## What ORBIT-X Teaches

ORBIT-X connects **computer programming with fundamental aerospace engineering concepts**.

It demonstrates how conditional logic, mathematical calculations, system monitoring, and predefined decision rules can model selected aspects of complex engineering operations.

The project is an educational simulation, not real spacecraft flight software. Its physics, thresholds, telemetry, and recovery procedures are intentionally simplified.

**ORBIT-X demonstrates how even fundamental programming concepts can help us understand the logic behind space exploration.**
